                        "form": "salaamed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                        "entry_id": "a38d9f21-2be3-3983-a6e8-35fac8faba1f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To perform a salaam to (someone)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9074080-66d4-4a3c-9840-931c70ad8590",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "[H]e went away salaaming, and protesting his friendship and his master’s goodwill."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df640c63-b730-4e66-9feb-e7d9bdb6bedf",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "He salaamed low to Flory, covering his face with his hand […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "724c8e47-a765-47a7-8489-1483572e8edd",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "Outside the town, three ragged children salaamed the Governor from the back of a camel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c29dbac6-2f5d-4606-804c-b4b8d330716f",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "Beside himself, his possibilities; / salaaming hours of a half-blind morning / while the rainy lepers salaamed back,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d96e8622-5f96-4154-82c2-336c2a1160c7",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "The tea-planters’ houses of Ceylon […] were often surrounded by admirable lawns of coarse mountain grass, upon which the planters’ ladies enviably sat, buzzed about by harmless insects and salaamed by passing serfs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01cbbb58-0f9a-409e-af53-da3cbf966d3a",
                                "sense_id": "f5f19c9b-7db2-32db-a624-f37aebfe0bf4",
                                "text": "Nantwich made a kind of diving or salaaming motion with his hands, and the man nodded and smiled."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
